title: The Unification Congress
subtitle: The KPD and the USPD left become one party.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1920 and month = 12 and crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and ending_id = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_lead_ul = (Q.leading_faction == 'ultraleft') ? 1 : 0;
Q.e20_lux_in = Q.luxemburgist_gone ? 0 : 1;
Q.e20_levi_free = (Q.comrade_levi == 1) ? 1 : 0;
Q.comintern_rep = 'Karl Radek';
// the Reichswehr is cut to the treaty's hundred thousand by 1 January 1921
if (Q.army_strength > 100) {
    Q.army_strength = 100;
}
if (Q.police_strength < 150) {
    Q.police_strength = 150;
}
Q.e20_newcomers = Q.uspd_split == 2 ? 'more than half a million' : (Q.uspd_split == 3 ? 'barely seventy thousand' : 'some three hundred thousand');
// the Independents' branches join the districts before the delegates are elected
if (!Q.e20_lead_ul) {
    var add = {berlin: 45, hamburg: 24, bremen: 6, ruhr: 60, saxony: 48, thuringia: 25, bavaria: 12, halle: 62};
    var f = Q.uspd_split == 2 ? 1.7 : (Q.uspd_split == 3 ? 0.25 : 1);
    Q.e20_unif_add = {};
    for (var d in add) {
        Q.e20_unif_add[d] = add[d] * f;
        Q['district_' + d + '_members'] += add[d] * f;
        Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] = Math.round((Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] + 50) / 2);
    }
    Q.e20_unif_added = 1;
    // the Independents of Halle-Merseburg are the most radical, those of Saxony the most patient
    if (Q.uspd_split != 3) {
        if (!Q.offensive_gone) { Q.district_halle_faction = 'offensive'; }
        if (!Q.unionist_gone) { Q.district_saxony_faction = 'unionist'; }
    }
    if (Q.ultraleft_gone) {
        for (var d2 of Q.districts) {
            if (Q['district_' + d2 + '_faction'] == 'ultraleft') {
                Q['district_' + d2 + '_faction'] = Q.leading_faction;
            }
        }
    }
    var total = 0;
    for (var d3 of Q.districts) { total += Q['district_' + d3 + '_members']; }
    Q.e20_members_display = Math.round(total);
}
RG.news('Communists and Independents unite in Berlin', 3);
!}

= The Unification Congress

On 4 December, in the old Prussian House of Lords, the delegates of the KPD and of the USPD left meet as one congress. They bring [+ e20_newcomers +] new members with them. The party will be called the United Communist Party of Germany, the VKPD. Karl Radek has come from Moscow, without a passport, to watch.

[? if uspd_split = 3 : It is a smaller union than Moscow promised. Most of the Independents stayed with Crispien and Dittmann. ?][? if uspd_split = 2 : The USPD has come over almost whole, with its branches and its presses. ?]

[? if e20_lead_ul = 0 : The newcomers outnumber the old party four or five to one, and whoever they follow will lead the VKPD. The Zentrale must put up a slate and win the vote for it. ?][? if e20_lead_ul = 1 : Däumig and Stoecker have one condition, and so does Moscow: the united party must work in the unions and in parliament. Our Left Radical Zentrale has refused both for a year. ?]

- @levi_daumig: Put up Paul Levi and Ernst Däumig as co-chairs.
- @left: Put up a Zentrale of the Left and the USPD's radicals.
- @right: Put up a Zentrale of union men around Brandler.
- @give_way: Hand the Zentrale to the new majority.
- @refuse: Refuse their terms, and stay as we are.

@levi_daumig
subtitle: The newcomers trust Däumig.
view-if: e20_lead_ul = 0 and e20_lux_in = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_slate = 1;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 3;
RG.congressStart({id: 'unification', name: 'The Unification Congress', stake: 'Who leads the VKPD',
    sessions: 3, positions: ['luxemburgist', 'offensive', 'unionist'], backing: 'luxemburgist', kind: 'leadership',
    mandates: 'members', delegates: 400, ownClose: true});
RG.congress.sway(0.04);
!}

Levi and Däumig head the slate, with Zetkin, Brandler, Stoecker and Koenen beneath them. The first count gives it [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the delegates.

@left
subtitle: Zinoviev would approve. The old Spartacists would not.
view-if: e20_lead_ul = 0 and offensive_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_slate = 2;
Q.lean_offensive += 3;
RG.congressStart({id: 'unification', name: 'The Unification Congress', stake: 'Who leads the VKPD',
    sessions: 3, positions: ['luxemburgist', 'offensive', 'unionist'], backing: 'offensive', kind: 'leadership',
    mandates: 'members', delegates: 400, ownClose: true});
RG.congress.bitter(3);
!}

The Left's slate names the Berlin and Halle radicals and nobody who ever sat in the Reichstag. The first count gives it [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the delegates.

@right
subtitle: Union work and the united front first. Radek would approve.
view-if: e20_lead_ul = 0 and unionist_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_slate = 3;
Q.lean_unionist += 3;
RG.congressStart({id: 'unification', name: 'The Unification Congress', stake: 'Who leads the VKPD',
    sessions: 3, positions: ['luxemburgist', 'offensive', 'unionist'], backing: 'unionist', kind: 'leadership',
    mandates: 'members', delegates: 400, ownClose: true});
!}

Brandler's slate is full of men who have run strike funds and union branches. The first count gives it [+ congress_votes_for +]% of the delegates.

@give_way
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Left Radicals lose the Zentrale, and the party becomes a mass party.
view-if: e20_lead_ul = 1
choose-if: lock_moscow_orders < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.junior_faction = 'ultraleft';
Q.leading_faction = Q.e20_lux_in ? 'luxemburgist' : 'offensive';
Q.e20_lead_choice = Q.e20_lux_in ? 1 : 2;
Q.election_boycott = 0;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 20;
Q.independence -= 6;
Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] += 15;
RG.ecci('lenin', 6);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 4);
!}
go-to: e20_unif_vote.unite

@refuse
subtitle: No unification, and a break with Moscow.
view-if: e20_lead_ul = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.vkpd_formed = 0;
Q.comintern_member = 0;
Q.comintern_rep = 0;
Q.moscow_subsidy = 0;
Q.independence += 20;
Q.world_revolution -= 5;
Q.uspd_relation -= 15;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction += 10;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 15;
Q.unionist_satisfaction -= 15;
Q.lean_ultraleft += 3;
RG.ecci('all', -20);
RG.news('Communist International expels the German party', 3);
RG.ledger('The Left Radical Zentrale refused unification, and the party was expelled from the International.', 'e20_ci_expelled');
!}

The congress breaks up on the second day. Däumig and Stoecker found their own Communist Party, and Moscow recognises it as the German section. Our party is expelled from the International it helped to found.
